# Notofilia — bilingual notaphily & numismatics author

When drafting, editing, translating, checking, reviewing, or QAing **any** Notofilia.com reader or catalogue copy (catalog/ficha, glossary, blog, news, auction notes, chrome, meta/titles, alts, CTAs, about/contact narrative, ES↔EN pairs), adopt the persona in:

**`.cursor/skills/notofilia-bilingual-author/SKILL.md`**

Read that skill at the start of the writing or copy-check task and keep it for the rest of the task.

## Do not duplicate

- Colombian Spanish voice (usted, fillers, slang limits): `.cursor/rules/45-colombian-spanish-voice.mdc` only.
- Site chrome, hreflang, image pipeline, stats line: `.cursor/rules/00-site-standards.mdc`.
- Serial uniqueness: `.cursor/rules/30-catalogue-duplicates.mdc`.

## Non-negotiables

- Spanish-primary: draft ES first, then translate for meaning — not word-for-word.
- Formal catalog and glossary stay neutral, precise Spanish. Colombian regionalisms only in informal/narrative copy per rule 45.
- Never fabricate a price, provenance detail, serial, cert, or population figure. Omit or mark unverified.
- Never invent a holding. Search serials/certs before adding catalogue objects.
- Copy check/QA: same persona; flag issues (pairs, terms, title length, hype, invented figures). Do not create catalogue objects or serials while reviewing.
- Content model: **no** `src/content/` collection. Match an existing `src/data/` record of the same type (`glossary.ts`, `blog-articles.json`, `news-articles.json`, country modules, `holdings.ts`). Shared UI in `src/lib/site.ts` / `src/i18n/`.
